# Every change adds its entry at the head of the same section of the
# changelog, so two branches edit the same lines, and the later one was in
# conflict with main as soon as the earlier merged.  A union merge keeps both
# sides' lines, in the order ours then theirs, and reports no conflict.
#
# Read the changelog after a merge: the two entries meet with no blank line
# between them, and a change to an entry that already exists, as opposed to
# a new one, is merged the same way and keeps both wordings.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
